      <!-- How to Calculate Fuel Cost -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>How to Calculate Fuel Cost for Any Journey</h2>
        <p>Calculating the cost of fuel for any car, motorcycle, or commercial vehicle requires three essential figures:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Total Travel Distance:</strong> The total length of your journey in kilometres (km) or miles (including the return leg if you are doing a round trip).</li>
          <li><strong>Vehicle Fuel Economy (Mileage):</strong> How far your vehicle can travel on a specific quantity of fuel (commonly expressed as <em>km/L</em>, <em>L/100 km</em>, or <em>MPG</em>).</li>
          <li><strong>Current Fuel Price:</strong> The actual pump price per litre or gallon for petrol (gasoline) or diesel at your local fuel station.</li>
        </ol>
