      <!-- Fuel Cost Formula -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>The Universal Fuel Cost Formula</h2>
        <p>The core mathematical equation connects distance, vehicle mileage, and price per litre into two simple steps:</p>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-4 border border-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800/60 dark:border-slate-700 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-2">
          <div class="font-bold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">Step 1: Total Fuel Required (Litres)</div>
          <div>Fuel Required (L) = Distance ÷ Fuel Economy (km/L)</div>
          <div class="pt-2 font-bold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">Step 2: Total Fuel Cost</div>
          <div>Total Fuel Cost = Fuel Required (L) × Fuel Price (per litre)</div>
          <div class="pt-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Combined Formula:</div>
          <div class="text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-bold">Total Fuel Cost = (Distance ÷ Fuel Economy) × Fuel Price</div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
          For European vehicles where consumption is measured in <strong>L/100 km</strong>, the formula adjusts to:
          <code>Fuel (L) = (Distance × L/100 km) ÷ 100</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- How to Calculate Fuel Cost Per KM -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>How to Calculate Fuel Cost Per KM (Kilometre)</h2>
        <p>Knowing your vehicle's <strong>fuel cost per km</strong> is invaluable for tracking running costs, comparing public transit vs driving, and billing client travel.</p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800/50">
          <div class="font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Formula:</div>
          <div class="mt-1 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            Fuel Cost per km = Fuel Price per Litre ÷ Fuel Economy in km/L
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            <em>Educational Example:</em> If petrol costs ₹100 per litre and your vehicle delivers 20 km/L, your running fuel cost is <strong>₹100 ÷ 20 = ₹5.00 per km</strong>.
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Similarly, your <strong>fuel cost per mile</strong> can be determined directly by multiplying cost per km by <strong>1.609344</strong>.</p>
